language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Minimum number of coins of each denomination so that every amount below the maximum can be paid exactly.
given denominations_dim1 : int(1..)
given denominations : matrix indexed by [int(1..denominations_dim1)] of int(1..)
given max_amount_to_pay : int(2..)
find x : matrix indexed by [int(1..denominations_dim1)] of int(0..max_amount_to_pay)
$ auxiliary: y[a,i] is how many coins of denomination i are used to pay amount a
find y : matrix indexed by [int(1..max_amount_to_pay), int(1..denominations_dim1)] of int(0..max_amount_to_pay)

branching on [x]
minimising (sum i : int(1..denominations_dim1) . x[i])
such that
$ every amount from 1 up to the maximum (not including it) can be paid exactly with the coins
forAll a : int(1..max_amount_to_pay-1) . ((sum i : int(1..denominations_dim1) . y[a,i] * denominations[i]) = a),
$ the coins used for any amount come from the coins available (no more than x[i] of denomination i)
forAll a : int(1..max_amount_to_pay-1) . forAll i : int(1..denominations_dim1) . (y[a,i] <= x[i])
